<title>UK: Reed rises on talk of Reuters bid.</title>
<headline>Reed rises on talk of Reuters bid.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Reed International Plc rose on Wednesday on renewed talk that the company could be the target of a bid from Reuters Holdings Plc, dealers said.</p>
<p>A spokesman for international news and information group Reuters declined comment, saying it was the company's policy not to comment on market rumour.</p>
<p>Shares in publishing firm Reed were up 47-1/2p at 11.50 stg by 1310 GMT in volume of 1.4 million shares.</p>
<p>Reuters was up 2-1/2p at 658 in volume of 3.8 million.</p>
<p>&quot;The rumours around Reed and Reuters just won't go away,&quot; said one dealer.</p>
<p>Reed was not immediately available for comment. -- London Newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
</text>
